    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d215">

                <pb facs="0280" n="188" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg188"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Moscow/257: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-12T12:00:00+03:00">November 12,
                        1943—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1925. Secret and personal for the Secretary from the Ambassador.</p>
                <p>Reference your 1180 November 9,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d215-f1"/> as authorized by
                    the Department I have had my letter of Nov. 10 to Molotov containing the President’s agreement concerning Turkey
                    attached as an annex to the Soviet-British protocol concerning Turkey signed by
                        Molotov and Eden on November 1 in Moscow.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d215-f2"/></p>
                <p>Since Molotov finally decided that the
                    above arrangement was preferable I did not insist on the protocol and annex
                    being incorporated in the secret military record of the conference.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harriman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
